## Problem

- **A tenant user who forgets their password cannot get back in.** The tenant user admin (`tenant_manage_users`) can create, list, update and deactivate users, but has no reset: `POST /api/tenant/users/{id}/password/reset` → 404. The MSSP reset `POST /api/mssp/users/{id}/password/reset` deliberately refuses tenant users (404). The account cannot be recreated either, because the e-mail stays taken (409). The only fix was `soctalk-auth set-password` inside the api pod.
- **The staff page has no "Reset password" button**, although the MSSP API exists (internal-auth §8.5).

## Fix

**API.** `POST /api/tenant/users/{id}/password/reset` (tenant_admin, `tenant_manage_users`). It runs under the caller's tenant RLS context with an explicit `user_type='tenant' AND tenant_id=<caller's tenant>` predicate, and locks the row. It calls `admin_reset_password`, which:

- sets `must_change`;
- clears the lockout and the sign-in rate limit;
- revokes all of the target's sessions;
- writes `auth.password.reset.admin`;
- returns the one-time password once.

Errors:

| Case | Answer |
|---|---|
| own account | 400 (use password change) |
| not a user of the caller's tenant (MSSP staff, other tenant, unknown) | 404 |
| deactivated user | 409 (reactivate first; otherwise the password would silently go live on a later reactivation) |
| proxy auth mode | 404 |

**UI.** "Reset password" on **Staff users** and on the tenant **Users** page.

- Hidden on your own row and for deactivated users. On the staff page it is also hidden on a `platform_admin` row unless you are one (the API answers 403 there anyway).
- A confirmation dialog shows the §8.5 text, then the one-time password once, with "Copy and close". The password lives only in the dialog's state and is gone when the dialog closes.

**Messages and docs.** Strings in all 7 locales; `docs/multi-tenant/internal-auth.md` documents the endpoint and §8.5 covers both pages.

